{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Stone Sour, Sevendust and One-X fit my interest in heavy riffs paired with melodic vocals, connecting naturally to Disturbed and Alter Bridge in my listening history.",
    "The Formation Of Damnation especially appeals to my appetite for aggressive riffs after Advance And Vanquish and Colony, while Black Gives Way To Blue fits the darker mood I enjoy in Tool."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Better Days Comin' feels more polished and melodic than the heavier, more aggressive music I want right now.",
    "I cannot confidently identify The Other Side, Duality or ProdName, so I lack a clear musical reason to choose them; that uncertainty does not mean I dislike their sound."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Sharing a broad hard-rock connection is not enough for me when the intensity and balance of riffs and melody differ.",
    "Explicit-lyrics labels do not explain my interest; heaviness, mood and vocal style matter more to my choices."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My listening includes a strong appetite for thrash and heavier metal, which makes The Formation Of Damnation more compelling than softer melodic hard rock right now.",
    "Interest does not always mean I would choose an album immediately: Transit Of Venus appeals to me, but One-X is the one I would try first."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations capture my interest in heavy music with melody, but sometimes overlook the intensity, mood and confidence in an album's identity that determine what I choose now."
}"}
